; Hypothetical for limit 03: what was written first in dijkstra.l0's
; heap_pop, and what the checker would ideally say about it.
;
; This IS valid L0 and gives the right answer; it copies the heap on every
; pop (dijkstra on the 10,000-node graph: 2.45 s instead of 0.25 s, 16
; billion words copied, every test still passing). What is missing is not a
; construct but a diagnostic. The compiler already knows, from its last-use
; analysis (spec 10.3), that h is used after the array_set that consumes it,
; so it could warn:
;
;   FILE:LINE:COL: warning: h is used after this array_set consumes it, so
;   it copies h; read what you need from h first
;
; Reordering is not an option: array_get can fail, so spec section 8 forbids
; moving it past the inner array_set, whose own failure it would then mask.

(def heap_pop ((h (array int)) (size int)) (array int)
  (let last (sub size 1)
    (sift_down (array_set (array_set h 0 (array_get h (mul 2 last)))
                          1 (array_get h (add (mul 2 last) 1)))
               0 last)))

(def sift_down ((h (array int)) (i int) (size int)) (array int) h)
